) | taken / not taken (`-0.0` does **not** take it) |\n| F. float value class | all arithmetic | normal, ±0.0, subnormal, ±inf, NaN, FLT_MAX/FLT_MIN extremes, overflow/underflow of `max-min` |\n| G. pointer relationship | 3–4, 21–23 & 35–37 | disjoint buffers / `dest == src` (in-place) / partially overlapping / unaligned-by-1-float views |\n\n## Table — one row per meaningful combination\n\nEvery row is exercised through **both** `.so` exports with many randomized\ninputs (fixed seed, `SplitMix64`) plus the listed edge constants, and the\n3 output floats are compared **bit-for-bit**.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `rgb_to_hsv` | disjoint buffers; r strictly max, g > b (sector D=r, E not taken, h ∈ (0,60)) — randomized in (0,1] | [ ] |\n| 2  | `rgb_to_hsv` | disjoint buffers; r strictly max, b > g (sector D=r, **E taken**, h ∈ (300,360)) — randomized | [ ] |\n| 3  | `rgb_to_hsv` | disjoint buffers; r max, g == b exactly (h == `+0.0`, E not taken) — randomized magnitude | [ ] |\n| 4  | `rgb_to_hsv` | disjoint buffers; g strictly max (sector D=g, h ∈ (60,180)) — randomized | [ ] |\n| 5  | `rgb_to_hsv` | disjoint buffers; b strictly max (sector D=b, h ∈ (180,300)) — randomized | [ ] |\n| 6  | `rgb_to_hsv` | tie r == g > b → sector priority must pick **r** (line 26 wins) — randomized | [ ] |\n| 7  | `rgb_to_hsv` | tie g == b > r → max ternaries keep g (strict `>`), sector picks **g** — randomized | [ ] |\n| 8  | `rgb_to_hsv` | tie r == b > g → sector picks **r** — randomized | [ ] |\n| 9  | `rgb_to_hsv` | all three equal, positive → guard C via `delta == 0` (early return, s stays 0) — randomized | [ ] |\n| 10 | `rgb_to_hsv` | all three equal to `0.0` → guard C via **both** disjuncts | [ ] |\n| 11 | `rgb_to_hsv` | max is exactly `0.0` while `delta != 0` (mixed zero/negative) → guard C via `max == 0`, division skipped — randomized negatives | [ ] |\n| 12 | `rgb_to_hsv` | all components negative, distinct → no guard, `s < 0`, all 3 sectors covered — randomized in [-1,0) | [ ] |\n| 13 | `rgb_to_hsv` | mixed-sign components (min < 0 < max) → `delta > max`, `s > 1` — randomized in [-1,1] | [ ] |\n| 14 | `rgb_to_hsv` | signed zeros: all 8 combinations of `±0.0` in (r,g,b) — pins `v`'s zero sign and the `delta == 0` disjunct | [ ] |\n| 15 | `rgb_to_hsv` | subnormal inputs (`1e-45`, `FLT_MIN/2`, …), incl. subnormal `delta` and subnormal `max` | [ ] |\n| 16 | `rgb_to_hsv` | extreme magnitudes: `FLT_MAX`, `-FLT_MAX`, `FLT_MIN`, overflow of `max - min` to `+inf` | [ ] |\n| 17 | `rgb_to_hsv` | non-finite: every placement of `+inf` / `-inf` over the 3 slots (3^3 combos of {-inf, +inf, 1.0}) | [ ] |\n| 18 | `rgb_to_hsv` | NaN: quiet NaN in each slot, several NaN payloads/signs, plus all-NaN (checks branch-false semantics and payload propagation) | [ ] |\n| 19 | `rgb_to_hsv` | 8-bit-quantised sRGB shape: components from `{0,1,…,255}/255` (the library's intended real input shape), exhaustive over a randomized sample | [ ] |\n| 20 | `rgb_to_hsv` | components ≥ 1 / large positive normals (h denominators large, s < 1) — randomized in [1, 1e6] | [ ] |\n| 21 | `rgb_to_hsv` | fully random bit patterns reinterpreted as `f32` (any class, incl. NaN/inf/subnormal) — 20 000 randomized cases | [ ] |\n| 22 | `rgb_to_hsv` | pointer relationship: `dest == src` (in-place) over randomized inputs from rows 1–5 shapes | [ ] |\n| 23 | `rgb_to_hsv` | pointer relationship: partially overlapping (`dest = buf`, `src = buf+1`) and (`dest = buf+1`, `src = buf`), randomized | [ ] |\n| 24 | `rgb_to_hsv` | pointer relationship: disjoint but **unaligned to 16 B** (`buf+1` … `buf+3` offsets) → no SSE-alignment assumption difference | [ ] |\n| 25 | `rgb_to_hsv` | output-window bound: `dest` inside a canary-guarded buffer → exactly 3 floats written, neighbours untouched | [ ] |\n| 26 | `rgb_to_hsv` | repeated / stateless invocation: 1 call, then 1 000 randomized calls reusing the same buffers, then re-running the first input → identical result (no hidden state) | [ ] |\n| 27 | `rgb_to_hsv` | batch/stride use: 4096-pixel array converted element-by-element through both `.so`s (composed pipeline over a whole image buffer) | [ ] |\n\n## Build configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`; `CMakeLists.txt` declares no options and\nthe C source has no `#ifdef`. Hence the cross-product of build configurations is\na single cell, and rows 1–27 are run under:\n\n| # | configuration | command |\n|---|---------------|---------|\n| 1 | default (== no features == all features) | `cargo test --no-default-features`, `cargo test --all-features`, `cargo test` |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3633,"cache_read_input_tokens":31792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3633,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe25812e-aedf-49e8-8ae7-c96ff11fb693","uuid":"7e14ce3f-6a04-40ac-87f5-abd21d1f9fb6","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:34:33.291Z"}
